WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.656 --> 00:00:05.138
I was lying on my bed one morning, thinking about how perfect everything was.

2
00:00:05.378 --> 00:00:08.520
Usually there is at least one thing wrong in my life.

3
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:15.723
Most days it has something to do with my brother, Tate.

4
00:00:28.448 --> 00:00:33.349
Yesterday, for example, he got mad when I squeezed all the toothpaste out of the tube.

5
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.631
I was experimenting to see if I could invent an automatic toothpaste squeezer.

6
00:00:40.671 --> 00:00:42.252
Or sometimes it's our dinner menu.

7
00:00:43.292 --> 00:00:49.514
I hate when Mom makes eggplant casserole, which is the most disgusting food ever invented.

8
00:00:50.514 --> 00:00:52.495
Whoever invented it should go to jail!

9
00:00:53.555 --> 00:00:55.816
But tonight we were having pizza.

10
00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:57.216
My favorite.

11
00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:59.902
Plus, winter vacation was coming up soon.

12
00:01:01.103 --> 00:01:04.385
So I was going to have a whole week to think up a new invention.

13
00:01:05.346 --> 00:01:10.269
If the invention was really good, I might even get into the Inventor's Hall of Fame!

14
00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.612
You'd better watch out when you think everything is perfect.

15
00:01:15.713 --> 00:01:16.654
Do you know why?

16
00:01:17.654 --> 00:01:21.737
Because that means something big is about to go wrong!

17
00:01:21.757 --> 00:01:25.020
"Iggy, the muffins are ready!"

18
00:01:25.532 --> 00:01:27.713
my mom called, knocking on my door.

19
00:01:27.733 --> 00:01:31.275
"And I have a surprise."

20
00:01:32.655 --> 00:01:35.677
Oh boy, warm muffins and a surprise!

21
00:01:35.697 --> 00:01:38.638
"What's the surprise?"

22
00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.279
I asked, coming out of my room.

23
00:01:41.419 --> 00:01:43.340
My brother Tate walked into the kitchen.

24
00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.861
"Is the surprise for me too?"

25
00:01:46.282 --> 00:01:46.842
he asked.

26
00:01:46.862 --> 00:01:49.663
"Sit down," Mom said.

27
00:01:49.683 --> 00:01:51.304
"And I'll tell you both."

28
00:01:52.524 --> 00:01:56.387
Tate and I each took a warm muffin and sat down at the table.

29
00:01:56.407 --> 00:02:04.052
"Well," she began, "last night I got a call from Aunt Julia and Uncle John."

30
00:02:04.072 --> 00:02:06.113
"That's great!"

31
00:02:06.554 --> 00:02:06.974
I said.

32
00:02:06.994 --> 00:02:10.436
"Are we going to visit them over winter vacation?"

33
00:02:11.417 --> 00:02:14.779
My aunt Julia and uncle John are super-rich.

34
00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.261
They live in a big house with a swimming pool.

35
00:02:19.282 --> 00:02:21.824
Of course, it's too cold to swim in the pool in the winter.

36
00:02:22.816 --> 00:02:26.739
"But maybe we can go sledding on the hill behind their house," I thought.

37
00:02:26.759 --> 00:02:31.423
"And I can work on my new invention in their huge attic!"

38
00:02:33.925 --> 00:02:35.487
Tate looked excited too.

39
00:02:35.507 --> 00:02:37.448
"Cool," he said.

40
00:02:37.468 --> 00:02:41.132
"I can stay in the bedroom with the TV like I did last year."

41
00:02:41.152 --> 00:02:47.217
"I hope I don't have to share a room with Oliver again," I said.

42
00:02:48.518 --> 00:02:50.700
My little cousin is a big pain.

43
00:02:51.828 --> 00:02:55.990
He never shares his stuff, and he is always complaining about something.

44
00:02:56.010 --> 00:03:04.055
"Well my mother said, "actually you will be sharing a room with Oliver, Iggy."

45
00:03:04.075 --> 00:03:06.336
"Too bad!"

46
00:03:06.796 --> 00:03:08.377
Tate said, grinning at me.

47
00:03:09.978 --> 00:03:10.538
I shrugged.

48
00:03:10.558 --> 00:03:12.599
"That's okay," I said.

49
00:03:12.619 --> 00:03:17.382
"I guess I can stand being stuck in Oliver's room for a few days."

50
00:03:17.402 --> 00:03:24.470
"You don't understand," my mom said, "we're not going to your aunt and uncle's house."

51
00:03:26.391 --> 00:03:27.251
"What do you mean?"

52
00:03:27.731 --> 00:03:28.212
I asked.

53
00:03:28.232 --> 00:03:31.133
"Are we all going on a trip together?"

54
00:03:31.153 --> 00:03:34.375
"No," my mom said.

55
00:03:34.395 --> 00:03:37.237
"Oliver is coming to visit us.

56
00:03:37.777 --> 00:03:39.638
He'll be sharing your bedroom, Iggy."

57
00:03:40.679 --> 00:03:43.140
"What?" I practically shouted.

58
00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:46.762
"Calm down, Iggy," said Mom.

59
00:03:46.782 --> 00:03:49.324
"It's only for a short time."

60
00:03:50.456 --> 00:03:52.257
"But why does he have to come here?"

61
00:03:52.277 --> 00:03:53.278
I asked.

62
00:03:53.298 --> 00:03:56.360
"And why does he have to share my room?

63
00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.201
Why can't he share with Tate?"

64
00:03:58.221 --> 00:04:00.382
"No way!"

65
00:04:00.822 --> 00:04:01.543
said Tate.

66
00:04:01.563 --> 00:04:03.584
"He can't share with me.

67
00:04:03.924 --> 00:04:05.125
I'm a teenager."

68
00:04:05.145 --> 00:04:09.248
"Well, I'm an inventor," I said.

69
00:04:09.268 --> 00:04:12.590
"And I'm on the brink of a major invention.

70
00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.152
It's going to win me a place in the Inventor's Hall of Fame!"

71
00:04:17.956 --> 00:04:20.557
You need quiet time to think up a great invention.

72
00:04:21.858 --> 00:04:24.499
I could forget about quiet time with Oliver around.

73
00:04:24.519 --> 00:04:29.881
"It will be fine, Iggy," my mom said.

74
00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:31.141
"You'll see."

75
00:04:31.161 --> 00:04:33.922
I saw something, all right.

76
00:04:35.283 --> 00:04:38.864
I saw that my winter vacation was going to be horrible.

77
00:04:40.165 --> 00:04:41.325
What did I tell you?

78
00:04:42.326 --> 00:04:46.628
When things seem perfect, something big always goes wrong!
